  "published": "2026-10-19T10:32:36.017Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "#### Added\n* Windows command-line length check. When the assembled command line exceeds the Windows\n  `CreateProcess` limit (~32,767 characters), you get an `ArgumentException` before the process\n  starts instead of Win32 error 206. Skipped when `UseShellExecute` is enabled.\n\n#### Fixed\n* `ProcessTimeoutPolicy.Enabled = false` now means no timeout in all three waits instead of\n  arming the kill timer anyway, and interrupt-task faults are always observed.\n* `MiddlewareContext.Next` invokes only the next middleware and the rest of the chain, not the\n  composed chain head, which previously caused unbounded recursion.\n* `AddCliInvoke` registers `IProcessConfigurationBuilder` as a blank-builder factory. The old\n  by-type mapping threw on every `GetService`.\n* `IExternalProcess.StartAsync(configuration, ct)` honors `RedirectStandardInput` like the\n  instance overloads. A configured writer with redirection disabled is a no-op in every path.\n* `FromProcessStartInfo` accepts empty-string environment values as a valid way to clear a\n  variable. Keys must be non-null and non-empty.",
